<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Islamic Republic of Afghanistan</h1><p class="st-meta">2001 CE – 2021 CE · capital Kabul</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Western-backed Afghan state that followed the Taliban's fall in 2001, holding elections and expanding education before collapsing in 2021.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the US-led invasion overthrew the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-1996-2001">Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan</a> (1996-2001), the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonn-agreement-2001">Bonn Agreement</a> of December 2001 created an interim administration under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamid-karzai">Hamid Karzai</a>. A loya jirga approved a new constitution in 2004, establishing the Islamic <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/democratic-republic-of-afghanistan">Republic of Afghanistan</a>, and Karzai was elected president.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic held presidential and parliamentary elections and expanded schools, healthcare and media, with millions of girls returning to school. It depended on foreign aid and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> forces, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-security-assistance-force">ISAF</a> mission. Corruption, disputed elections, opium production and a growing Taliban insurgency weakened it. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashraf-ghani">Ashraf Ghani</a> succeeded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamid-karzai">Karzai</a> in 2014, sharing power with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-abdullah">Abdullah Abdullah</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the US-Taliban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doha-agreement-2020">Doha agreement</a> of 2020 and the withdrawal of foreign troops, the Taliban took provincial capitals rapidly. Ghani fled on 15 August 2021, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> fell, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-1996-2001">Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan</a> (2021-present) was restored.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/islamic-republic-of-afghanistan.jpg" alt="Islamic Republic of Afghanistan" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Fry1989 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Afghanistan_(2004%E2%80%932021,_variant).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>2001 CE – 2021 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kabul</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hamid Karzai, Ashraf Ghani</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Pashto, Dari</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Afghan Transitional Administration, Afghan Interim Administration</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2011&amp;focus=islamic-republic-of-afghanistan" aria-label="Islamic Republic of Afghanistan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6437 927 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Islamic Republic of Afghanistan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6757 1183L6757 1183M6757 1183L6757 1183"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6757 1183h0M6757 1183h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6757 1183h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6757 1183h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kabul. <a href="/atlas?year=2011&amp;focus=islamic-republic-of-afghanistan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
